# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  .env.example — TEMPLATE. Copy to `.env.local` and fill in real values.
#
#      cp .env.example .env.local
#
#  `.env` and `.env.*` are gitignored (except this file), so real values never
#  travel via git. That is correct for secrets — but it also means a fresh clone
#  or a SECOND MACHINE starts with none of them, and features that depend on
#  them fail there while working fine on the machine that has them. That is
#  exactly how the feedback button broke: "The public key is required".
#
#  IMPORTANT — REACT_APP_* are BUILD-TIME values.
#  Create React App inlines them into the bundle when you build. They are NOT
#  read at runtime. So every place that BUILDS the app needs them:
#
#    • local dev  → this file as `.env.local`, then restart `npm start`
#                   (CRA reads env only at startup — a save won't pick it up)
#    • production → Cloudflare Pages → Workers & Pages → aira-monte-carlo →
#                   Settings → Variables and Secrets → add each one, then
#                   REDEPLOY. Setting them changes nothing until a new build.
#
#  Anything REACT_APP_* ends up readable in the shipped JavaScript. Only put
#  values here that are safe to be public. Server-side secrets
#  (STRIPE_SECRET_KEY, JWT_SECRET, ADMIN_SECRET, GEMINI_API_KEY) belong in
#  `.dev.vars` for `wrangler pages dev`, and in the Cloudflare dashboard for
#  production — never here.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── Feedback button (EmailJS) ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# All three are required together; with any one missing the feedback dialog
# reports that it is not configured rather than attempting a doomed send.
#
# Public key   → EmailJS dashboard → Account → General → "Public Key"
#                (called USER_ID here for historical reasons; it is the public
#                key, and it is designed to be public — it ships in the bundle)
REACT_APP_EMAILJS_USER_ID=

# Service ID   → EmailJS dashboard → Email Services → your service
REACT_APP_EMAILJS_SERVICE_ID=

# Template ID  → EmailJS dashboard → Email Templates → your template
REACT_APP_EMAILJS_TEMPLATE_ID=
